From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: sm8550: preserve the encoded UniPro divider

F() stores an encoded HID divider. clk_rcg_set_rate() takes an integer
divisor, encodes it again and ORs it into the previous divider. Thus the
300 MHz frequency result can disagree with the actual hardware clock.
Replace the old divider/source/mode fields with the frequency-table values
and trigger the update. This is the SM8550 counterpart of the previously
verified SM8450 fix, limited to the local UniPro clock implementation.

Frequency table and register source:
https://github.com/ianchb/sm8550-mainline/blob/ad75da348a020f0b7cb541ca2f06ab38cf77004d/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clock-sm8550.c
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
 		freq = qcom_find_freq(ftbl_ufs_unipro, rate);
-		clk_rcg_set_rate(priv->base, 0x77098, freq->pre_div, freq->src);
+		clrsetbits_le32(priv->base + 0x7709c,
+			       GENMASK(4, 0) | GENMASK(10, 8) |
+			       GENMASK(13, 12) | BIT(20),
+			       freq->pre_div | freq->src);
+		clk_bcr_update(priv->base + 0x77098);
 		return freq->freq;
